1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:05,861
Welcome, detective! Let us use numbers to prepare our school fair.

2
00:00:06,200 --> 00:00:12,592
Two hundreds, three tens, and six ones make two hundred thirty-six.

3
00:00:12,732 --> 00:00:16,468
It is greater than two hundred thirty.

4
00:00:16,608 --> 00:00:20,876
Compare the place values, starting with the hundreds.

5
00:00:21,200 --> 00:00:22,827
Addition joins amounts.

6
00:00:22,967 --> 00:00:26,737
Twenty-seven plus fifteen is forty-two.

7
00:00:26,877 --> 00:00:31,183
Exchange ten ones for one ten when needed.

8
00:00:31,323 --> 00:00:34,021
Subtraction takes an amount away.

9
00:00:34,161 --> 00:00:39,003
Forty-two minus fifteen returns us to twenty-seven.

10
00:00:39,143 --> 00:00:42,377
The operations help check each other.

11
00:00:43,200 --> 00:00:48,041
Three bags with five pencils each make fifteen pencils.

12
00:00:48,181 --> 00:00:50,880
That is multiplication: equal groups.

13
00:00:51,020 --> 00:00:55,861
Sharing fifteen equally among three bags gives five each.

14
00:00:56,001 --> 00:00:57,629
That is division.

15
00:00:57,769 --> 00:01:02,074
Check that every bag has the same number.

16
00:01:03,200 --> 00:01:05,363
Multiples follow equal jumps.

17
00:01:05,503 --> 00:01:08,201
Count in threes or fives.

18
00:01:08,341 --> 00:01:14,790
Fifteen appears in both patterns, so one number can fit two rules.

19
00:01:16,200 --> 00:01:19,904
Fractions describe equal parts of a whole.

20
00:01:20,044 --> 00:01:23,748
One of four parts is one quarter.

21
00:01:23,888 --> 00:01:26,540
Two quarters make one half.

22
00:01:26,680 --> 00:01:29,858
Three shaded parts make three quarters.

23
00:01:30,200 --> 00:01:35,041
Three thousand plus four thousand costs seven thousand rupiah.

24
00:01:35,181 --> 00:01:36,809
Pay ten thousand.

25
00:01:36,949 --> 00:01:42,496
How much change?

26
00:01:42,686 --> 00:01:46,861
Three thousand: subtract the cost from your payment.

27
00:01:52,200 --> 00:01:56,506
Read, choose your method, and check your answer.

28
00:01:56,646 --> 00:01:59,344
Try the Unit One quizzes!
